+# Glossary
+
+- **On-hand**: physical units of a SKU in a warehouse. Derived from the
+  `Ledger`, never stored.
+- **Allocated**: units promised to `PLACED` orders that have not shipped yet.
+  Does not include holds.
+- **Reservation / hold**: a temporary claim on available stock for a cart
+  during checkout. It is `ACTIVE` until it is confirmed (it becomes an order),
+  released, or it lapses at `expires_at`. See [ADR 0001](docs/adr/0001-lazy-reservation-expiry.md).
+- **Held**: units in `ACTIVE`, not-yet-lapsed reservations.
+- **Available**: `on_hand - allocated - held`, floored at zero. This is what new
+  orders and new holds may take.
+- **Lapse / expired**: a hold whose `expires_at` has been reached (instant
+  included). It stops counting as held at that moment, with no sweep needed.
+- **Partial fill**: a reservation holds, per line, as many units as are available,
+  up to what was asked. Lines with nothing available are left out. See
+  [ADR 0002](docs/adr/0002-partial-fill-reservations.md).
+- **Idempotency key**: a caller-chosen key that makes `reserve` safe to retry. The
+  same key with the same request returns the original reservation. See
+  [ADR 0003](docs/adr/0003-reservation-idempotency.md).
