index 0000000..380f8bb
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/adr/0003-reservation-idempotency.md
@@ -0,0 +1,16 @@
+# 0003 — Reservation idempotency keys are global and permanent
+
+Status: accepted (2026-10-29)
+
+## Decision
+- A key is taken by a successful `reserve` only. Failed calls leave it free.
+- Keys are global (not per warehouse) and never expire, even after the
+  reservation is confirmed, released or lapsed.
+- The same key with the same warehouse and the same requested items returns the
+  original reservation in its current state, and never moves `expires_at`. The
+  same key with anything else raises `IdempotencyConflict`.
+
+## Consequences
+- After a hold lapses, the cart must use a new key to hold again.
+- The key index grows without bound. That is acceptable for the in-memory
+  repository, but a persistent one will need a retention decision.
